cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ICU Edge-to-FHIR Interoperability Gateway"
abstract: >-
  An open-source research implementation of an edge gateway that converts ICU
  bedside monitor data (HL7 v2.x) into HL7 FHIR R4 resources, applies
  physiological bounds checking and waveform artifact rejection (notch,
  Butterworth bandpass and Hampel filtering), and computes the National Early
  Warning Score 2 (NEWS2) deterministically. Developed under IEC 62304 software
  life-cycle practices with ISO 14971 risk analysis. Research software only;
  not a medical device.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Abouelreish"
    given-names: "Housam"
    affiliation: "Mansoura University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/abouelre-maker/ICU-Edge-Gateway"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
keywords:
  - HL7 FHIR R4
  - HL7 v2
  - NEWS2
  - early warning score
  - intensive care unit
  - biomedical signal processing
  - artifact rejection
  - healthcare interoperability
  - software as a medical device
  - IEC 62304
  - ISO 14971
